      "no_parameter_transform_errors",
      "no_optimizer_runtime_errors"
    ],
    "note": "Matches M0/M1_stimulus_kernel's own convergence tolerances; no_probability_normalization_errors is dropped because this evaluator has no renormalization step -- pi_t is a convex combination of pi_{t-1} in [0,1] and A_t in {0,1} (the mouse's own valid choice) with weight alpha in the open interval (0,1), so it is bounded in [0,1] by construction, and the evaluator additionally raises immediately if pi_t is ever non-finite (see action_core_v1/evaluator.py)."
